In article <ll!j9ak@lynx.unm.edu> emullins@triton.unm.edu (Eric Mullins) writes:
>1-easy
>2-hard
>3-extrahard
Stupid idea! There are 12 different characters. The difficulty of the game
should only be affected by the character you choose. I propose to remove the
HARD option and add some things that depends on the character and that can
not be changed during the game (par example: remove the potion of gain
ability). Or introduce an other, real luck that can't be changed during the
game. Some characters should be to clumsy to pile objects in such way that
they can be polymorphed. Give the Samurai the ability to identify weapons
automatically. This is a real advantage, but there are still many people who
are not ascended yet. The weaker characters should also be difficult after they
have found a beehive, a good weapon and good armor. Many nasty things should be
introduced in hell for these characters.

There is no reason to introduce more HARD options as long as the 12 characters
are only different the first 10 dungeon levels.

